 R←Test_Table_006(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;Tbl;cells;markdown;newCursorCol;cells2;markdown2;newCursorCol2
⍝ `FormatTable` formats a plain table, and formatting an already formatted table changes nothing
⍝ R gets one of: 0=Okay, 1=test case failed, ¯1=test case was not executed due to the "batchFlag"
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 R←T._Failed

 Tbl←##.Meddy.Tables
 (cells markdown newCursorCol)←Tbl.FormatTable('| Name | Qty |' '|---|---|' '| a | 1 |')0 2
 →T.PassesIf('|Name|Qty|' '|----|---|' '|a   |  1|')≡markdown
 →T.PassesIf 3 2≡⍴cells
 →T.PassesIf 2≡newCursorCol

 ⍝ Feeding the result back in must not change it any more
 (cells2 markdown2 newCursorCol2)←Tbl.FormatTable markdown 0 2
 →T.PassesIf markdown≡markdown2
 →T.PassesIf cells≡cells2

 R←T._OK
⍝Done
